  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_039, 0.7250) uses scVI as the RNA encoder with ViT-L, transformer aggregation, and weighted fusion in a multiprofile multimodal setup. We have strong evidence that learned RNA representations (scVI) outperform linear ones (PCA) by ~1-4 points across settings, but scGPT—a generative model-based encoder—has never been tested in any multimodal configuration. This is the largest remaining source of uncertainty about the RNA encoder choice. Question: Does scGPT match or exceed scVI in the optimal multimodal pipeline? Why this experiment: config_051 (scgpt, ViT-L, transformer, weighted, multiprofile) is a single-variable swap from the current best (config_039), isolating the RNA encoder effect. A positive result would identify a new promising direction; a negative result would confirm scVI as the best RNA encoder and redirect budget toward other levers (e.g., fusion refinements or additional image encoders). Under a limited budget, resolving this high-impact uncertainty with a clean A/B comparison is the most efficient use of the next experiment."
}

